# Copy this file to `.dev.vars` and fill in the values below.
# `.dev.vars` is gitignored; this `.example` is committed as a shape reference.
# These bindings are used by `wrangler dev` locally. For deploys, use
# `wrangler secret put <NAME>` instead — secrets are encrypted by Cloudflare
# and never appear in source.
#
# Any value may be a literal OR a 1Password secret reference of the form
# `op://<vault>/<item>/<field>`. `scripts/push-secrets.sh` resolves references
# via the `op` CLI at push time (needs `op signin` or OP_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_TOKEN)
# and leaves literals untouched, so you can keep secrets out of the file:
#   MS_CLIENT_SECRET=op://Private/MS To-Do MCP/credential
# Surrounding quotes are stripped, so 1Password's "Copy Secret Reference"
# (which includes double quotes) can be pasted in verbatim.

# Microsoft Entra app registration — Azure portal → App registrations → your app
MS_TENANT_ID=
MS_CLIENT_ID=
MS_CLIENT_SECRET=

# The mail or userPrincipalName of the Microsoft account whose To Do data this
# server reads/writes. The /authorize default handler rejects any signed-in user
# whose /me response doesn't match this value (case-insensitive).
OWNER_EMAIL=
